## Q3 �?" the text

**Boundary paragraph** (replacing "WHAT THIS FILE'S CHECKS CAN AND CANNOT SEE" through "Inside the boundary:"):

> WHAT THIS FILE'S CHECKS CAN AND CANNOT SEE.  Every check here reads state this file writes (the tallies, the call counts, `rows', sc_g) or output this file prints, so an edit that reproduces a healthy run's observables -- by skipping rows and printing what they would have printed, by writing what a check reads, or by rewriting the log after the rows have run -- is invisible to all of them.  That boundary is a fact about in-file checks, not a gap in this block.  Two things cross it: a gate-side run on a device that fails a covered row -- one capacity row through row_cmp() AND one ring row through chk(), each on its own device mutant, because a skip of one group leaves the other group's lane green, and a lane closes only the rows its mutants fail (filed: `wdcidlane') -- and the log reaching the gate through a pipe rather than a seekable file, which no exit handler can rewrite (filed with it).  Inside the boundary:

**(A)**, replacing its first sentence and appending one:

> (A) THE COMPARATORS ARE PINNED -- the probes require the exact change in `failures' and cmp_fails on their own calls, so an inert comparator, or one narrowed on values the probes present, is caught at one end of the run or the other.  Not caught, measured: any difference between what a comparator does on a probe call and on a real call -- a test keyed on a value, a name, a position or this block's phase that the probes do not share; a predicate rewritten to agree with the original on every probe and differ elsewhere (the sum of the two gots against twice the want, say); and the code that FEEDS a comparator (row() handing row_cmp() its own want).  "Comparator" means its compiled behaviour: a file-scope macro that rewrites a printf or a name inside it is an edit of the comparator, wherever the line sits.

**(B)**, in full:

> (B) A COVERED FAILURE REPORTS ITSELF -- on a non-probe mismatch each comparator prints a line gate 2's failure-count check reads (`N failures so far'), at the moment it fails; that check compares every such line in the log against "0", so once the line is in the log no edit of the tallies, the trailer or the rows' order takes it back, and no line matching the check can be added without reddening it.  Hence no edit that leaves the covered rows running and the comparators' compiled behaviour intact hides a covered failure: not the trailer's count, token or exit rewritten singly or together, not a reset of either tally or both at any placement, not rows moved or deferred past the verdict with their counts forged (measured: #551f's pass, regress/artifacts/wdcidselfcheck_20260925/measured/run551f.out and opus551_measured_f/analyze9.out, gate 2's own lib.sh and selfmutant.py).  Not caught -- the (A) residual reaching the report: the report kept from the check on real calls (its guard switched off, its text moved off the pattern, or its printf swallowed by a file-scope macro) together with the tallies hidden (a reset, or the rows deferred past the trailer) -- and both halves can be ONE edit (a guard that also undoes the increments; the macro).  No other line in this file may print `<digits> failures': one that does reds every healthy run, loudly.

**(C)**, in full:

> (C) OBSERVABLES FORGED -- a row that does not run cannot report, and a log rewritten after the rows have run reports nothing.  Skipping the ring rows while printing their gate-pinned labels and adding 24 to `rows' and chk_calls is one insertion and green (measured); an exit handler that seeks a file-redirected stdout to 0 and writes a healthy log over the real one is one insertion and [green -- measured / walked, not measured] (M19, #551f's pass).  The identity row's 128 and the LAST run's call counts raise the cost of a skip; nothing in this file raises the cost of a rewrite.  That is the boundary's own class; its close is `wdcidlane' and the pipe.

**Gate-2 bullet**, replacing from "'Covered' means" to "`wdcidcomparators'.":

> "Covered" means the COMPARATOR is live, not that a row is.  What this file's checks can see stops at what the file itself writes.  CAN keep this gate green -- measured on #551's passes, disclosed, not chased: any difference between a comparator's behaviour on the self-check's calls and on real calls (a keyed or probe-agreeing test, feeding it its own want, or its failure report kept from this gate's count check while the tallies are hidden -- one edit or two, in the comparator's text or through a file-scope macro); an edit of the self-check itself; and the observables forged (covered rows skipped with their labels and counts printed, or the log rewritten by the process after the rows ran).  Anything else -- a trailer rewrite, a reset of either or both tallies anywhere, rows moved or deferred with their counts forged -- is caught: a covered failure prints a line this gate's `[0-9]+ failures' check reads at the moment it fails.  The file covers 24 comparisons and reports all 32 comparator failures.  The gate-side close is a lane whose device mutants fail one capacity row and one ring row, and the log read through a pipe (filed: `wdcidlane').  #551, by owner ruling 2026-09-25 ("24/128 now, file the rest"); the rest is `wdcidcomparators'.

