regress/artifacts/wdcidselfcheck_20260925/pass551e/fable5_pass551e.md:30:Right in substance. Contents: (1) the emission, in both failure arms after `cmp_fails ++`: `if (name[0] != '@') printf("  FAIL  covered comparator failure -- %d failures so far\n", cmp_fails);` (`why[0]` in `row_cmp()`). Print `cmp_fails`, which is at least 1 at that point; the text must carry no gate-pinned label, no "high byte", no geometry text, no `@@SELFCHECK@@`. (2) The pin kept, its comment rewritten: "a second identity constant — it catches covered rows skipped or moved without their counts forged, and like the identity row's 128 it is forgeable by an edit that writes the counter; change with the rows." Its measured delta survives emission (delete the ring rows and re-pin the identity: red with the pin, green without), so the addition licence holds. (3) The contract, (4) H7's caption, (5) H5/H6 records. A floor-bound diff; it owes its own pass.
regress/artifacts/wdcidselfcheck_20260925/pass551e/fable5_pass551e.md:34:> WHAT THIS FILE'S CHECKS CAN AND CANNOT SEE. Every check here reads state this file writes (the tallies, the call counts, `rows', sc_g) or output this file prints, so an edit that reproduces a healthy run's observables is invisible to all of them. That boundary is a fact about in-file checks, not a gap in this block, and only a gate-side run on a device that fails a COVERED row sees across it (filed: `wdcidlane', on the FIRST covered row). Inside the boundary: (A) THE COMPARATORS ARE PINNED -- the probes require the exact change in `failures' and cmp_fails on their own calls, so an inert or narrowed comparator is caught at one end of the run or the other. Not caught, measured: a test inside a comparator keyed on a value, a name, a position or this block's phase that the probes do not share; a predicate rewritten to agree with the original on every probe and differ elsewhere (the sum of the two gots against twice the want, say); and the code that FEEDS a comparator (row() handing row_cmp() its own want). (B) A COVERED FAILURE REPORTS ITSELF -- on a non-probe mismatch each comparator prints a line gate 2's failure-count check reads (`N failures so far'), at the moment it fails; that check compares every such line in the log against "0", so a printed line cannot be taken back and no line can be added. Hence no edit that leaves the covered rows running and the comparators intact hides a covered failure: not the trailer's count, token or exit rewritten singly or together, not a reset of either tally or both at any placement, not rows moved or deferred past the verdict with their counts forged (measured: #551f's pass, <artifact>). Not caught: that report switched off for non-probe calls -- its guard is itself a probe/real key -- together with an edit that hides the tallies. (C) A ROW THAT DOES NOT RUN CANNOT REPORT -- the identity row's 128 and the LAST run's call counts (chk() 24, row_cmp() 8) raise the cost of skipping covered rows, and both are values this file can forge: skipping the ring rows while printing their gate-pinned labels and adding 24 to `rows' and chk_calls is one insertion and green here. That is the boundary's own class; its close is `wdcidlane'. (D) This block itself. Nothing this block prints carries the self-mutant row's text, "high byte" or a pinned label. Gate 2's G text is printed ONCE, by the last run, only when both runs passed; the run's PASS needs that line (sc_g) and both tallies at zero; a probe failure forces one failure, and a missing first run is counted by the trailer's `!sc_g' line. Reviewed in the differential, not chased. The rest of the file is filed as `wdcidcomparators' (#551; owner ruling 2026-09-25).
regress/artifacts/wdcidselfcheck_20260925/pass551e/fable5_pass551e.md:38:> "Covered" means the COMPARATOR is live, not that a row is. What this file's checks can see stops at what the file itself writes: a keyed or probe-agreeing test inside a comparator, feeding a comparator its own want, that comparator's own failure report switched off, an edit of the self-check, or covered rows skipped with their labels and counts forged CAN keep this gate green -- measured on #551's passes, disclosed, not chased; the close is a lane whose device mutant fails the first covered row, filed as `wdcidlane'. Any edit that leaves the covered rows running and the comparators intact is caught: a covered failure prints a line this gate's `[0-9]+ failures' check reads at the moment it fails, so no trailer rewrite, reset or deferral hides it; the last self-check pins the comparator call counts; the run's PASS needs the G line and both tallies at zero. The file covers 24 comparisons and reports all 32 comparator failures. #551, by owner ruling 2026-09-25 ("24/128 now, file the rest"); the rest is `wdcidcomparators'.
regress/artifacts/wdcidselfcheck_20260925/pass551e/fable5_pass551e.md:42:It overturns the REASON and keeps the narrow claim. My premise — everything gate 2 reads is produced at one call site — is measured false: the count check reads the whole log, so a comparator can report to gate 2 at the moment it fails. "A pin on the trailer cannot survive" stands (J2). The class did not merely move into class (1); it split: the report switched off for real calls (class 1, irreducibly — the guard is a probe/real key, the class no probe set closes) and the rows not run (class C, the boundary's own). What changed materially: before J3, two edits confined to `main()` hid a covered failure; after J3, every hiding edit must touch a comparator's failure arm or stop the row running — the residual now sits exactly on the boundary theorem, which is why the contract must state that theorem rather than list members.
regress/artifacts/wdcidselfcheck_20260925/pass551e/fable5_pass551e.md:48:None of the acceptances reverses its finding; two are incomplete: H1's revision dropped the boundary statement, and H2 conflated tamper-detection today with liveness against a future defect. Missed by everyone including me: (1) the (C) single insertion under emission — skip `row_ring_occupancy_sound()`'s body while printing its gate-pinned labels and adding 24 to `rows` and `chk_calls`: no emission, pin satisfied, identity satisfied, lane intact; grok named its synchronous variant in passing and nobody scored it. It must be measured in #551f's pass and named in the contract, because it is the theorem's member, not a gap. (2) The all-matches semantics of the count check, which nobody wrote down: it is why emission works, why nothing can be forged in, and why the '@' guard must keep healthy logs at exactly one match. (3) H6's consequence for the record: the 8 verdict-handed calls report through the emission, so "24 covered" and "32 reported" are both true and must both be said. (4) The two goals in H2 were never separated in any pass's record; separating them is what stops the next pass re-litigating glm's argument against J3. Astra confirms after 07:01; nothing commits before then.
