regress/artifacts/wdcidselfcheck_20260925/pass551d/fable5_pass551d.md:25:Both readings are half right. The composites are not floor breaches, so the trigger clause ("breaches in two consecutive passes") is not met — but the amendment exists to stop exactly this shape (b→c repaired the tally, c→d the verdict, d finds the trailer open two sites over), and "disclose the class" must not become the way to dodge a closable class. The question is whether the trailer class is closable in-file. It is not: everything gate 2 reads is produced at one call site in `main()`, a probe cannot pin a call site, and any single-call-site helper is inlined away by one edit (that is what kills G17's closure). A source pin in gate 2 would pin the verdict's text and still admit a conditional both-tally reset inserted above it. The only close that reads the OUTPUT under a covered defect is F15's covered-row lane — gate-side, outside the owner-ruled scope, correctly filed. So the trailer becomes CONTRACT, honestly worded (Q3), and the chain does not stay open for it.
regress/artifacts/wdcidselfcheck_20260925/pass551d/fable5_pass551d.md:33:> NOT CAUGHT, DISCLOSED. This block pins the two COMPARATORS and nothing else: it proves they answer right on ITS OWN calls, so an edit that keeps those answers and changes the rest CAN keep every gate-2 row green. Four classes, each measured on #551's passes: (1) inside a comparator, a test keyed on a value, a name, a position or this block's own phase that the probes do not share, or a predicate rewritten to agree with the original on every probe and differ elsewhere (the sum of the two gots against twice the want, say -- one member of a class no finite probe set closes); (2) the code that FEEDS a comparator (row() handing row_cmp() its own want); (3) THE TRAILER, one call site: the printed count, the PASS token and the exit status are produced there, and any rewrite that keeps them consistent with each other is green -- today two coordinated edits, each red alone (the verdict's cmp_fails term dropped with `failures -= cmp_fails' after the reconciliation; the verdict and the printed count both scoring `failures - cmp_fails'); a reset of BOTH tallies is in this class -- unconditional, only after the covered rows and before the self-mutant's row; conditional on their equality, anywhere. No in-file probe can pin a single call site; the close is gate-side, a lane whose device mutant fails the FIRST covered row (filed: `wdcidlane'); (4) this block itself (a probe's cmp_fails check weakened together with the increment it guards and a reset). A reset of `failures' alone is not among them, wherever it sits: the comparators also count cmp_fails, which only they increment, and the verdict and the exit status read it directly. Nor is moving the covered rows past the verdict: the LAST run requires chk() 24 and row_cmp() 8 calls. On #551d's pass no single edit outside these four classes kept gate 2 green (24 measured: regress/artifacts/wdcidselfcheck_20260925/opus551_measured_d/analyze6.out). Reviewed in 