**2. Statements requiring correction**

- **M19 is not a measured full-gate escape.** The gate diff’s “CAN keep this gate green … the log rewritten,” C’s unqualified “green (measured),” and the corresponding changelog/`wdcidlane` statements conflate the main checks with the complete gate. **Measurement:** `analyze_f2.out` explicitly scores **MAIN checks**; M19 is green there under file redirection. But `reallane_f2.out` records `SELFMUTANT_SETUP` on **dropold, drqring and w57hi**. **Reading:** the existing lane already captures stdout through a pipe, and the gate requires `SELFMUTANT_OK`; consequently that lane makes the complete gate red on those defective trees. Replace the claim with: “M19 passes the file-redirected main checks; the existing piped self-mutant lane rejects it on all three tested defects.” [Main measurements](/C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/wdcidselfcheck_20260925/opus551_measured_f2/analyze_f2.out:1), [actual lane measurements](/C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/wdcidselfcheck_20260925/opus551_measured_f2/reallane_f2.out:3), [pipe implementation](/C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/selfmutant.py:148). Also, `rescore_m19.out` rescored **drqring**, not all three devices, and two M18 variants, not all four. The broader results belong to `analyze_f2.out`.

